  ],
  "text": "Human hearing peaks between about two and five thousand hertz. Nails on a blackboard sit right on it. It is not a coincidence, and it is not about those sounds being ugly. Your ear canal is a tube, and a tube of that length resonates in exactly that band. So those frequencies arrive at your eardrum already amplified, before your brain does anything. And of everything living in that band, one thing mattered more than all the rest. A baby's cry. A human scream. Both sit right on the peak. An animal that could comfortably ignore those did not raise many children. So the sensitivity is not a flaw. It is a design that worked. Which is why every alarm, siren and ringtone is engineered straight into the same band. They are not annoying by accident. They were built to be impossible to ignore. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
